\section{Where the tutorials live}

The tutorials must be found from an installed wheel, not only from a
checkout, so their directory is derived from the location of this
module rather than from the working directory or a configuration
option.
The directory sits beside [[cli]] in the package, which keeps the
[[cli]] package free of data files and lets the tutorials be built by a
Makefile of their own.

<<functions>>=
def bundled_tutorial_dir():
  """Returns the directory of the tutorials shipped with canvaslms"""
  return pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "tutorials"
@

The layout is easy to break silently, by a packaging rule that drops
the Markdown files, for instance, so we check that the directory is
inside the installed package and holds at least one tutorial.

<<test helpers>>=
def bundled_tutorial_files():
  """Returns the Markdown tutorials shipped with canvaslms"""
  return sorted(tutorial.bundled_tutorial_dir().glob("*.md"))
@

<<test functions>>=
def test_bundled_dir_is_inside_the_package():
  """The tutorials ship with the package and hold at least one file"""
  package_dir = pathlib.Path(canvaslms.__file__).resolve().parent
  bundled = tutorial.bundled_tutorial_dir()

  assert bundled.is_dir()
  assert bundled.is_relative_to(package_dir)
  assert bundled_tutorial_files()
