\section{Which tutorials are offered}
\label{sec:tutorial-offered}

When pytorial is embedded it puts its own [[using-tutorials]] lesson
first in the catalog, before the host's tutorials, so that a learner
who has never met the runner learns [[list]], [[run]] and [[review]]
before anything specific to the host.
That lesson, however, was written against pytorial's standalone
catalog: its first step checks that [[tutorial list]] shows
[[shell-basics]] and [[writing-tutorials]], and its second step runs
[[shell-basics]].
Neither is mounted by an embedded host, so the very first tutorial our
users see would be one they cannot complete.\footnote{%
  Reported upstream as \url{https://github.com/dbosk/pytorial/issues/27}.}

Until that is fixed upstream we mount those two built-in tutorials as
well, after our own, so that every tutorial in the list can be finished.
We ask pytorial for its built-ins and leave out the universal one, which
[[add_argparse_subcommand]] will prepend on its own; listing it twice
would be a duplicate-identifier error.

<<functions>>=
def offered_tutorial_paths():
  """Returns the tutorial paths mounted under the tutorial command

  The bundled canvaslms tutorials come first, followed by pytorial's
  own built-in lessons except the universal one, which pytorial
  prepends itself.
  """
  universal = pytorial.catalog.universal_tutorial_path()
  companions = tuple(
    path for path in pytorial.catalog.builtin_tutorial_paths()
    if path != universal)
  return (bundled_tutorial_dir(),) + companions
@

A catalog built from these paths must load, which also proves that no
two tutorials share an identifier and that no path is missing.

<<test functions>>=
def test_offered_tutorials_build_a_catalog():
  """All offered paths exist and their identifiers are unique"""
  catalog = pytorial.catalog.TutorialCatalog(
    tutorial.offered_tutorial_paths())
  ids = [item.id for item in catalog.get_tutorials()]

  assert "getting-started" in ids
  assert "using-tutorials" not in ids
  assert len(ids) == len(set(ids))
